// Port of the historic test1.pme (Old Test-PostMachine's Compill
// compiler, 2007) — the only surviving artifact of that generation's
// code generator. The 12-byte image decodes (big-endian length word,
// then code) to `left; right; jmp 0` plus the compiler's auto-appended,
// unreachable stop marker: a codegen smoke test that loops forever.
// Preserved as-is — the program deliberately never terminates, so its
// test asserts the step-limit trap rather than a final tape.
main() {
    1: left;
    right;
    goto 1;
}
